@@ -225,12 +225,25 @@
   0 MB_N_R sc!
   0 MB_N_O sc!
   0 MB_N_A sc! ;
+\ Cache values invariant during this follower's neighbour scan. WANT is not
+\ used until sch-want resets it; PERP is not used until sch-turn writes it.
+\ R2 is shared with the separate startle scan, which sets its own radius.
+\ Refresh for EACH follower: sparse updates commit immediately, so later fish
+\ must still see earlier fish's freshly committed state, in the same order.
+: sch-scan-cache
+  MB_X me sch@ MB_PERP sc!
+  MB_Y me sch@ MB_PERP 1 + sc!
+  MB_Z me sch@ MB_PERP 2 + sc!
+  MB_WANT heading>sc
+  reach2 MB_R2 sc! ;
 : sch-follow
-  MB_ME sc!
+  dup MB_ME sc!
   clear-sums
+  sch-scan-cache
   sch-n 0 do
-    i me <> if i sch-pair then
+    i over <> if i sch-pair then
   loop
+  drop
   sch-walls sch-want
   sch-startle? if
     sch-startle-away
